sorry, i don't know whether any of these have been mentioned before or
not (since i haven't been very good about reading rec.games.nethack).
Anyone, this is a collection of things that i've seen that i consider
minor bugs (one with a fix), hardly worth mentioning:

1) The new identify command "/" sometimes does strange things.  A pice
	of food was indicated, and it said "a piece of food (rocks)", apparently
	because the food was a corpse that had decayed away after i had last
	visited it.  the ex-food was halfway across the screen.

2) The line of code in doeat() in eat.c that contains:

	if ( otmp->otyp != FORTUNE_COOKIE &&
		 ( otmp->cursed ||
		   ( ( ( monstermoves - otmp->age) > otmp->blessed ? 50 : 30) &&
		     ( otmp->orotten || !rn2(7))))) {

	is incorrect, since the "( monstermoves - otmp->age) > otmp->blessed"
	is evaluated before the ?: operator is.  instead of:

		   ( ( ( monstermoves - otmp->age) > otmp->blessed ? 50 : 30) &&

	the correct code is (of course):

		   ( ( ( monstermoves - otmp->age > otmp->blessed) ? 50 : 30) &&

	the affect of this (since otmp->blessed is a bit field) is to
	give all corpses a 1 out of 7 chance of being rotten, rather than
	just a 1 out of 7 chance of being rotten after 30 or 50 turns.
	(what's a blessed corpse like, anyway?)

3) "Blind" doesn't always show up on the status line immediately (when
	you put on a blindfold).  It waits for the next status line update.


this is nethack 3.0 patch level 7, on a 386 PC running AT&T SVR3.2

